---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Danny Silva | Public Notebook" activeNav="home">
    <!-- ── HERO ── -->
    <section class="hero" id="top">
        <div class="hero-content">
            <div class="hero-label fade-up">Public notebook</div>
            <h1 class="fade-up d1">Fragments from a mind trying to <em>pay attention.</em></h1>
            <p class="hero-desc fade-up d2">
                A quiet place for what I am thinking through: philosophy, art, technology, books, experiments, attention, and the work of becoming a little less distracted.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-buttons fade-up d3">
                <a href="/blog" class="btn btn-primary">Enter the Notebook
                    <svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg>
                </a>
                <a href="/about" class="btn btn-ghost">Why This Exists</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── ABOUT ── -->
    <section id="about" class="about-section">
        <div class="about-content">
            <p class="fade-up d2">
                I'm <strong>Danny</strong>. This is where I leave traces of what I am noticing before it hardens into an opinion: ideas from books, small philosophical arguments with myself, art that lingers, tools I am building, and ordinary days that teach something.
            </p>
            <p class="fade-up d3">
                Technology is part of the notebook because it is part of my life, but it is not the whole point. The real subject is attention: where it goes, what it makes possible, and what it costs.
            </p>
            <p class="fade-up d4">
                Read it as a conversation with myself that happens to be public.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
